<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main id="main-content">
  <section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><%= page.kind === 'privacy' ? 'Privacy' : 'Terms' %></li></ol></nav><p class="eyebrow">Amicus Shipping LLC</p><h1><%= page.kind === 'privacy' ? 'Privacy notice' : 'Website terms' %></h1></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container legal-content">
  <% if (page.kind === 'privacy') { %>
    <p>This notice describes how the Amicus Shipping corporate website works. The eSIM store and other linked applications have their own privacy information.</p>
    <h2>Contact details you provide</h2><p>When you submit the inquiry form, this website validates your name, email, selections and message, then sends them to Amicus through our configured email provider. The website does not keep inquiries in a database. Messages are handled in the company inbox and by the email providers involved so we can respond to your inquiry.</p><p>The form confirms when the email service accepts a message. If sending is unavailable, it shows an error and a direct contact option. Avoid including payment card details, passwords, passport copies or eSIM activation codes.</p>
    <h2>Site usage and technical information</h2><p>The production site uses our existing analytics service at analytics.amicusshippingllc.com to understand page visits and clicks on key links. Our event hooks include only an event name and page path; they exclude contact fields, message text and query strings. The analytics service may process technical visit information such as the page, browser, device and referring site.</p><p>The corporate application does not set login or advertising cookies. Short-lived request information, including IP addresses, is used in server memory to limit repeated form submissions. Hosting and proxy services may keep technical request logs separately.</p>
    <h2>Your choices and questions</h2><p>You can contact us directly instead of using the form. The configured tracker is instructed to respect the browser’s Do Not Track setting. For a question about your information or to request its correction or deletion, email <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>.</p>
  <% } else { %>
    <p>This website introduces Amicus Shipping LLC and provides routes to connectivity, crew tools and maritime resources.</p>
    <h2>Information and resources</h2><p>Guides on this site provide general preparation information. Check the current instructions for your device, plan, provider or operational process before acting. A study tool does not issue a qualification or replace official training requirements.</p>
    <h2>Separate services and purchases</h2><p>Purchases take place in the dedicated eSIM store or another clearly linked service. Review that service’s current product details, coverage, eligibility, pricing and terms before placing an order. A link from this website does not guarantee availability or establish a service booking.</p>
    <h2>Inquiries</h2><p>The contact form sends your inquiry to Amicus. A successful submission means our email service accepted the message; it does not confirm transport, connectivity provisioning, a response time or another commercial arrangement.</p>
    <h2>Using the site</h2><p>Please do not misuse the forms, attempt unauthorized access or submit harmful content. Public file uploads are not offered. If you find an error or want to discuss a service, <a href="/contact">contact Amicus</a>.</p>
  <% } %>
  </div></section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
